@startuml approval-sequence
!include sequence.iuml
title LazyFinance — Explicit Proposal Approval\nExact saved version, atomic result and durable receipt

actor "Account owner" as Owner
participant "Action card\n(browser)" as Web <<boundary>>
participant "Actions service\n(API)" as API <<application>>
participant "Private persistence" as P <<persistence>>
database "PostgreSQL 18" as DB

note over Web, P : A bounded proposal is already saved. No financial change has been applied.
Owner -> Web : Review / edit exact card; choose Approve
Web -> API : approve(id, version)
activate API #D5E8D4
API -> P : Read current owned proposal
activate P #FFE6CC
P --> API : Saved request / version / state
deactivate P
API -> API : Normalize with current financial policies
API -> P : apply(id, version, normalized command)
activate P #FFE6CC
P -> DB : Begin transaction + per-owner write lock
activate DB #FFE6CC
note over P, DB : Recheck owner, completed turn, version, expiry and factual fingerprint.
alt Current valid proposal
  P -> DB : Domain commands + dependent tags + receipt
else Stale / expired proposal
  P -> DB : Finalize ledger state; no financial write
end
DB --> P : Commit one authoritative outcome
deactivate DB
P --> API : Applied receipt or current proposal state
deactivate P
API --> Web : Confirmed action state
deactivate API

ref over Web, P
  If the response is lost: explicitly read action status.
  Never automatically replay the mutation.
  Repeated approval returns the saved receipt, not another write.
end ref
note over API, DB : No model call during approval. Receipts survive chat deletion.
@enduml
